  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'slow travel' has gained popularity in recent years, particularly among environmentally conscious tourists. Proponents argue that it allows for a more authentic experience of the local culture and reduces the negative impacts associated with mass tourism. By staying in one place for an extended period, travelers can immerse themselves in the community, learn about traditional practices, and develop meaningful relationships with locals.\n\nIn contrast to the fast-paced and often superficial nature of mainstream tourism, slow travel encourages a more mindful approach to exploration. It involves taking time to appreciate the subtle nuances of a place, its history, and its people. This type of travel also fosters a sense of responsibility towards the environment and the local economy.\n\nHowever, some critics argue that slow travel can be elitist, as it requires a certain level of financial resources and flexibility. They claim that this approach excludes many potential travelers who cannot afford to take extended breaks or are constrained by work or family commitments.\n\nDespite these criticisms, the slow travel movement continues to grow in popularity. As more people become aware of its benefits, they are beginning to adopt this more sustainable and enriching way of exploring the world.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The negative impacts of mass tourism\", \"The benefits of slow travel for local economies\", \"The concept of slow travel and its growing popularity\", \"The criticisms of slow travel as an elitist approach\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is one of the advantages of slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It allows tourists to visit multiple places in a short time\", \"It enables travelers to immerse themselves in local culture and develop meaningful relationships with locals\", \"It reduces the financial burden on tourists\", \"It eliminates the need for language skills\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"The article mentions that slow travel can be criticized for being elitist. What is one reason given for this criticism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It requires a high level of physical fitness\", \"It demands a certain level of financial resources and flexibility\", \"It excludes people with disabilities\", \"It promotes the use of public transportation\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the author's attitude towards slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They are strongly opposed to it and see it as a waste of time\", \"They view it as a viable alternative to mainstream tourism, but acknowledge its limitations\", \"They believe it is the only responsible way to travel\", \"They think it is too expensive for most people\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"The author mentions that slow travel 'fosters a sense of responsibility towards the environment and the local economy'. What does this suggest about the author's purpose in writing the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To persuade readers to adopt mainstream tourism practices\", \"To inform readers about the concept of slow travel and its benefits\", \"To entertain readers with stories of exotic destinations\", \"To criticize the environmental impact of mass tourism\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
